    'parent.title': 'BloomType — Help Your Child Learn to Type at Home',
    'parent.hero': '<div class="free-badge">✨ Completely Free — No Credit Card Required</div><h1>Help Your Child Learn to Type with <span>BloomType</span></h1><p>A magical garden typing adventure for kids ages 6–11. No boring drills — just flowers, pets, and fun word games that build real keyboard skills.</p><a href="./index.html" class="cta-btn">🌸 Start Playing Now — It\'s Free!</a>',
    'parent.problemTitle': 'Why Typing Matters Now',
    'parent.problems': '<div class="problem-card"><div class="emoji">📚</div><h3>Schools Assume They Know</h3><p>Teachers assign online essays and tests, but kids never get formal typing instruction. They hunt-and-peck for years.</p></div><div class="problem-card"><div class="emoji">⏱️</div><h3>Homework Takes Forever</h3><p>A 10-minute assignment takes 45 minutes because they cannot find the keys. Frustration builds.</p></div><div class="problem-card"><div class="emoji">😫</div><h3>“Practice Websites” Are Boring</h3><p>Adult typing tutors are dry, timed, and stressful. Kids quit after 2 minutes.</p></div>',
    'parent.howTitle': 'How BloomType Works',
    'parent.features': '<div class="feature"><h3>🌼 Every Word Restores a Meadow</h3><p>Each word your child types grows a flower. As they finish a level, bees, butterflies and birds come back to the meadow. Mistakes never take anything away.</p></div><div class="feature"><h3>🐱 A Pet Cheers Them On</h3><p>A friendly flower-pet reacts to every keystroke. “Nice!” for correct letters. Gentle encouragement for mistakes.</p></div><div class="feature"><h3>🎹 10 Built-In Lessons</h3><p>Starts with home row (ASDF). Gradually adds top row, bottom row, capitals, and numbers. Each level takes 5–10 minutes.</p></div><div class="feature"><h3>🏆 Progress They Can See</h3><p>The garden grows as they play. Stars collect. Levels unlock. Kids feel proud of visible progress.</p></div>',
    'parent.curriculumTitle': 'What They Will Learn (10 Levels)',
    'parent.curriculum': '<div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">🌸</div><h3>Home Row Garden</h3><p>ASDF JKL; — finger placement</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">⬆️</div><h3>Top Row Sky</h3><p>QWERTYUIOP — reaching up</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">⬇️</div><h3>Bottom Row Ocean</h3><p>ZXCVBNM — reaching down</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">🌲</div><h3>All Letters Forest</h3><p>A–Z mixed practice</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">🏙️</div><h3>Capital City</h3><p>SHIFT + key technique</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">🚀</div><h3>Number Galaxy</h3><p>0123456789</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">⚡</div><h3>Speed Meadow</h3><p>Faster pace, combo chains</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">🎯</div><h3>Accuracy Peak</h3><p>Precision focus</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">✨</div><h3>Master Valley</h3><p>Challenge words</p></div><div class="level-preview"><div class="level-icon">🏆</div><h3>Legend Kingdom</h3><p>Final quest with everything</p></div>',
    'parent.preview': '<h3>📊 Parents Can Track Progress</h3><p>When your child plays on this device, you will see their WPM (words per minute), accuracy, and completed levels. No account is needed — progress saves automatically.</p><div class="stat-row"><div class="stat-pill">⚡ 12 WPM</div><div class="stat-pill">🎯 94% Accuracy</div><div class="stat-pill">🌸 Level 4 Reached</div><div class="stat-pill">⏱️ 45 Minutes Played</div></div><p style="margin-top:16px;font-size:0.85rem"><a href="./teacher.html" style="color:var(--primary-light)">Open Progress Dashboard →</a></p>',
    'parent.privacyTitle': 'What BloomType Stores',
    'parent.privacy': '<h3>Default local play</h3><p>BloomType stores the student’s chosen display name and avatar, scores, lesson progress, achievements, garden, practice history, class code, and accessibility preferences in this browser. It does not send that progress to BloomType or Ashbi while cloud sync is disabled.</p><h3>What we do not collect</h3><p>The game has no advertising, analytics, behavioral profiling, or third-party tracking SDKs. It does not ask students for an email address, birth date, home address, precise location, or free-form messages.</p><h3>Delete local progress</h3><p>Open <strong>Profile</strong> in the game and choose <strong>Delete local progress</strong>. This removes that student’s profile, progress, and local class membership from this browser. Clearing site data in the browser provides a second deletion path.</p><h3>Download progress</h3><p>Open <strong>Profile</strong> and choose <strong>Download local progress</strong> to save this browser’s student profile as a JSON file. An approved authenticated school deployment also shows a separate download for that signed-in student’s cloud profile, session history, and roster membership.</p><h3>School cloud deployments</h3><p>Cloud sync remains disabled in the public deployment. In an approved authenticated school deployment, the profile screen also offers cloud-progress deletion; it removes the student’s profile, session, and roster records and signs this browser out. The school must still provide its approved identity-account, backup-expiry, consent, retention, access, security, and account-isolation processes before storing real student data.</p><h3>Questions</h3><p>Email <a href="mailto:cameron@ashbi.ca?subject=BloomType%20privacy">cameron@ashbi.ca</a>. These product controls reduce risk but are not a claim of legal compliance for every school or region.</p>',
